      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "+1 so we can get access to it's manual update method, as well.\nWith Cinemachine (mostly) being used with cameras that output to render textures. In some cases, it may be more performant to manually update these cameras to cap their framerate. In this scenario, it makes sense to also call ManualUpdate() on the CinemachineBrain in time with camera.Render() for performance [+ because not doing this could possibly break things like motion vectors(?)]",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
